{
  "_readme": [
    "Wall planes for the room-scheme plates.",
    "",
    "Each plate is one real OPUDA'S photograph. Each plane is a surface that can be",
    "repainted: a clip polygon in fractions of the image, plus flood-fill seeds and a",
    "colour tolerance. The fill follows cornices, sockets and door frames, so the edge",
    "on the page follows the edge of the wall.",
    "",
    "The polygons were traced against each photograph with a 100-pixel grid overlay.",
    "If a mask ever comes out empty the build stops: a silently unpainted wall is worse",
    "than a failed build. Add 'whole': true for a surface with no flat region to fill.",
    "",
    "Order matters: schema entries are painted in this order, and each scheme supplies",
    "one hex per plane in the same order."
  ],
